# Ideation round 20260905T0200Z — coordinator synthesis (Astra's first round; four blind lanes: Astra, Grok, Fable, Opus)

Submissions: astra (45KB), grok46 (49KB), fable5 (49KB), opus5 (47KB); coordinator blind submission committed pre-read.

## 1. THE UNIFICATION (4/4 convergence): the RECEIVER is the universal object
All four independently name the same next object: the MONOMIAL-JACOBIAN RECEIVER — polynomial pairs (P,Q) in k[γ,π] with J(P,Q) = c·γ^k and a Newton-polygon bound (Fable: deg_γ[π^k] ≤ 3k for k=1) — and the SOURCE→RECEIVER ATLAS that maps every charged branch to its receiver with certificate pullbacks and an honest UNASSIGNED output (Astra). This SUBSUMES the prior frame:
- Fable: the k=1 RECEIVER carries 671/1110 of the D≤200 residue, the WHOLE K16 ray, AND the (8.1) atom — one object, three clients.
- Grok: the 14 Moh rows are s'=3 receivers → build the s'=3 MONOMIAL-JACOBIAN COMPILER (Appendix II extended by Φ_eff), NOT an Abel identity, NOT a 166-group order-chart sweep.
- Opus: the (K,ℓ)-lattice FIBRED over ℓ, with the (F3') divisibility per ray — "does every ray carry Φ | Gee?"
- Astra: the certificate-bearing receiver atlas is the single most valuable object; the routing maps (first-separation, route-to-state, coverage) are a SEPARATE interface obligation that CANNOT be collapsed into integer invariants — this is the real all-degree gap, not K16 and not the census.

## 2. Corrections to the packet (banked)
- The finite Moh residual is 12 rows in 6 full characteristic-data classes, NOT 14/7 (Astra: 2 of the 14 already die under the promoted Xu screen). All 12 have descended depth s' ≥ 3 (Grok/Opus: the s'=3 shape).
- The u_s≥2 census sharpened cohort compresses 296 → 132 on the four-integer key, NOT ~65 (Astra); and the four-integer key MERGES different inherited characteristic sequences — equality of four integers is NOT a proof of shared kill; a shared kill needs a PROVED COMMON NECESSARY RECEIVER (the atlas). So the "(K,ℓ)-lattice 4.6× compression" is a coarse index, not a kill-sharing theorem.
- Q2 was mistyped as an order-chart sweep (Grok): the 14 rows need the s'=3 compiler.
- Q4's reduction: (H1)∧(H2) is not a proof of plane JC2 without the routing/coverage maps (all four); the (K,ℓ) lattice is the right s_eff=2 ARCHITECTURE but not the coverage proof.

## 3. K16 — two concrete new levers (both cheap, replace the exhausted routes)
- Fable EXACT SQUARE: stop chasing the radical; the banked exponent at t=3,4 is 2, so prove τ_t² ∈ I_{t,+} with cofactors supported on the top-tail rows — a uniform-identity target of the kind the ray has yielded three times (spine, RESIDUAL-ZERO, TOP-TAIL-UNIT). The top-down ODE recursion is RESONANCE-FREE for all t≥3 except exactly the banked failure fibre (t,d)=(2,−1)=y=1/5 (pivots p_j = 2ω(4t+1−j)+2α, vanish only at j=6d(2d+1)). Cheapest decisive test: lift(I_{t,+}, τ_t²) at t=3,4,5, read the cofactor support (<30 min). Framing: (8.1) = "the chart cannot tilt the critical line off Moh's γ-axis" — the SAME object as the u_s=1, ℓ=1 receiver (so K16 ⊂ the k=1 receiver).
- Astra LINKED QUARTIC FACTORIZATION with a differential constraint (avenue 29/38 reopened): change the mechanism from undifferentiated polynomial-solution classification to a quartic product identity with a differential factor; root valuations of the linked quartic (avenue 38, narrow) are the coefficient-sensitive client.

## 4. Dispositions and launches
1. K16 EXACT SQUARE (Fable's τ_t² lever, cheapest decisive K16 test): LAUNCHED k16-exact-square-fable5.
2. The s'=3 MONOMIAL-JACOBIAN COMPILER for the 12 Moh rows (Grok): LAUNCHED moh-sprime3-compiler-grok46 — generates the s'=3 receiver charts (Appendix II × Φ_eff); the FLEET runs them (Moh ≤100 finish = generate + parallel-solve).
3. The k=1 RECEIVER + source→receiver atlas (Astra, primary — the unifying object): LAUNCHED receiver-atlas-k1-astra (build the receiver k[γ,π] J=c·γ, deg_γ[π^k]≤3k; the source→receiver homomorphism with certificate pullback + UNASSIGNED; validate on the 132-key cohort and the K16/(8.1) instance).
4. QUEUED: PROP-5.4-MINIMALITY (Fable, 1 lane-hour — does the program cover plane JC2 for MINIMAL counterexamples, settling scope?); the s'=3 compiler's charts → fleet batch.
STOP: the naive order-chart sweep for the 14 rows; treating the (K,ℓ) 4-integer key as a kill-share.

## 5. OPENs raised: OPEN[RECEIVER-ATLAS] (source→receiver coverage — the all-degree gap), OPEN[K16-TAU-SQUARE] (τ_t²∈I_{t,+}), OPEN[K16-LINKED-QUARTIC], OPEN[SPRIME3-COMPILER] (the 12 Moh rows), OPEN[PROP-5.4-MINIMALITY] (scope), OPEN[ROUTING-MAPS] (first-separation/route-to-state, not collapsible to integers).

