## 2. Q1 — K16: quotient the weak target by its intrinsic scaling coordinate

**Answer type: NEW REDUCTION PROVED-HERE; uniform emptiness OPEN.** Attack (8.1) directly. I would not commission another undirected EN nonzerodivisor lane. Cohen–Macaulayness and the length split identify a sharp object, but they have not supplied the missing coefficient-sensitive nonvanishing. The new mechanism is a canonical affine quotient of the exact nonvanishing locus, followed by an exhaustive elimination of the coefficient b.

### 2.1 First repair the socle inference

Let A_t=S_t/I_{t,+}, w_t=4t+1, and suppose A_t is finite-dimensional with top nonzero weight s_t. Then

"'```text
N_t := min{N≥1 : τ_t''^N=0 in A_t}
      ≤ floor(s_t/w_t)+1.
